after:
```typescript
function failureText(failure: unknown): string {
  try {
    throw failure;
  } catch (error) {
    if (error instanceof Error) {
      return error.message;
    }
    return "Not an Error object";
  }
}
console.log(failureText(new Error("Door closed")));
```
This prints `Door closed`. `instanceof Error` checks whether the caught value is an `Error` object. This small example throws a value on purpose so you can practise catching it.
